    <bpmn:process id="W_W3938" name="W3938. AI Explainability, Transparency &amp; Customer Disclosure" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Adverse-decision model (links to W3931); transparency need
Frequency: Per model + on adverse decision
Volume: Explainability for tier-1/customer-affecting models
Owner: AI Governance / Responsible AI
Participants: AI Governance, Data Science (links to VS-30.2), Legal (links to VS-100), Privacy (links to VS-91), CX (links to VS-13), business AI owners (fraud VS-125, credit VS-38)
Source: workflow W3938 — AI Explainability, Transparency &amp; Customer Disclosure</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3938_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3938_Lane1" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3938_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3938_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3938_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3938_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3938_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3938_Start3" name="Adverse-decision model (links to W3931); transparency need">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3938_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3938_Task4" name="AI Governance/Data-Science provide model explainability appropriate to impact…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/Data-Science provide model explainability appropriate to impact: global (feature importance) and local (per-decision reasons) for adverse decisions — fraud decline (links to VS-125), credit decline (links to VS-38), pricing, and LP flags (links to VS-23)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Data Science
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Per model</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3938_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3938_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3938_Task5" name="AI Governance/Legal/CX provide customer-facing transparency and reason-codes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance/Legal/CX provide customer-facing transparency and reason-codes for adverse automated decisions (RA 10173 automated-decision rights — links to VS-91), and a human-review channel (links to W3941)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Legal / CX
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Per decision type</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3938_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3938_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3938_Task6" name="AI Governance maintain model cards / documentation (purpose, data, performance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AI Governance maintain model cards / documentation (purpose, data, performance, limitations, intended use) per model (links to W3931), and ensure disclosure is accurate and not misleading
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Data Science
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Per model</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3938_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3938_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3938_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3938_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3938_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-615 (ensure controlled execution — Responsible AI — Fairness, Explainability, Privacy &amp; Safety (PA-128.2).) | - operational: explainability requirements; operational: accuracy control
Owner: AI Governance / Responsible AI</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
