    <bpmn:process id="W_W3939" name="W3939. AI Data Governance, Privacy (RA 10173) &amp; Consent for Profiling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: AI use of personal data; profiling/automated decision
Frequency: Per use-case + ongoing
Volume: AI data-use governance across all PII-touching models
Owner: AI Governance / Privacy
Participants: AI Governance, Privacy/DPO (links to VS-91), Data Governance (links to VS-29/VS-28.2), Legal (links to VS-100), Security (links to VS-27.3), business AI owners (CDP VS-126, fraud VS-125, personalization VS-126/W3892)
Source: workflow W3939 — AI Data Governance, Privacy (RA 10173) &amp; Consent for Profiling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3939_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3939_Lane1" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3939_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3939_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3939_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3939_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3939_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3939_Start3" name="AI use of personal data; profiling/automated decision">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3939_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3939_Task4" name="AI Governance/Privacy run a DPIA for AI/ML processing personal data (profiling…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/Privacy run a DPIA for AI/ML processing personal data (profiling, personalization, fraud scoring, CV/face — links to VS-91/W389), establish lawful basis and purpose-limitation, and register high-risk processing with NPC where required
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Privacy / Legal
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead / DPO
Duration: Per use-case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3939_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3939_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3939_Task5" name="AI Governance/Privacy ensure AI profiling/automated decisions have valid…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance/Privacy ensure AI profiling/automated decisions have valid consent or lawful basis under RA 10173 (links to VS-91/W3885 CDP consent center), honor objection/DSAR rights (links to VS-126/W3900), and minimize/pseudonymize PII in training/inference
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Privacy / Data Science
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead / DPO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3939_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3939_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3939_Task6" name="AI Governance/Data-Governance govern AI training data quality/lineage (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AI Governance/Data-Governance govern AI training data quality/lineage (links to VS-28.2/VS-29), prevent unlawful re-use (e.g., scraping customers&#x27; data into models), and document data provenance per model
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Data Governance / Data Science
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3939_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3939_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3939_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3939_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3939_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-147 (ensure AI model risk &amp; human-oversight control.) | - operational: DPIA and consent; operational: minimization and testing
Owner: AI Governance / Privacy</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3939_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3939_Annotation8" targetRef="W3939_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
