    <bpmn:process id="W_W3940" name="W3940. AI Safety, Robustness &amp; Adversarial/Failure Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Model deployment (links to W3932); failure/adversarial event
Frequency: Per model + continuous
Volume: Safety/robustness for tier-1 models
Owner: AI Governance / Data Science
Participants: AI Governance, Data Science (links to VS-30.2), Model Risk (links to VS-21), Security (links to VS-27.3), business AI owners, IT (links to VS-27)
Source: workflow W3940 — AI Safety, Robustness &amp; Adversarial/Failure Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3940_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3940_Lane1" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3940_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3940_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3940_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3940_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3940_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3940_Start3" name="Model deployment (links to W3932); failure/adversarial event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3940_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3940_Task4" name="AI Governance/Data-Science test model robustness: edge cases, distribution…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/Data-Science test model robustness: edge cases, distribution shift, data quality degradation (links to VS-28.2), failure modes, and define fail-safe behavior (fallback to rules/human — links to W3941) for safety/revenue-critical models (forecast VS-127, fraud VS-125, pricing)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Data Science / Model Risk
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Per model</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3940_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3940_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3940_Task5" name="AI Governance/Security govern adversarial-AI threats: prompt…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance/Security govern adversarial-AI threats: prompt injection/jailbreak (GenAI), data poisoning (training), model evasion (fraud links to VS-125), model theft/extraction, and membership inference (privacy links to VS-91)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Security / Data Science
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
