    <bpmn:process id="W_W3944" name="W3944. AI Regulatory &amp; Standards Monitoring (ISO 42001, NIST AI RMF, future PH AI rules)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Regulatory/standards change; compliance cycle
Frequency: Continuous + annual
Volume: AI regulatory radar + standards alignment
Owner: AI Governance / Compliance / Legal
Participants: AI Governance, Compliance (links to VS-22), Legal (links to VS-100), Privacy (links to VS-91), Government Affairs (links to VS-104), Risk (links to VS-21), Data Science (links to VS-30.2)
Source: workflow W3944 — AI Regulatory &amp; Standards Monitoring (ISO 42001, NIST AI RMF, future PH AI rules)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3944_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3944_Lane1" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3944_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3944_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3944_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3944_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3944_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3944_Start3" name="Regulatory/standards change; compliance cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3944_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3944_Task4" name="AI Governance/Compliance/Gov-Affairs monitor the AI regulatory and standards…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/Compliance/Gov-Affairs monitor the AI regulatory and standards landscape: ISO/IEC 42001 (AI Management System), NIST AI RMF, OECD AI Principles, and emerging PH/regional AI regulation (NPC guidance on automated decisions links to VS-91, potential PH AI act), and assess impact
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Compliance / Govt Affairs
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3944_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3944_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3944_Task5" name="AI Governance/Compliance align the AI program to standards (ISO 42001…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance/Compliance align the AI program to standards (ISO 42001 certification readiness where valuable, NIST AI RMF functions: govern/map/measure/manage), and close gaps (links to W3936 maturity)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Compliance / Risk
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3944_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3944_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3944_Task6" name="AI Governance/Legal/Gov-Affairs engage regulators/industry associations on AI…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AI Governance/Legal/Gov-Affairs engage regulators/industry associations on AI policy (links to VS-104), and prepare for future compliance (registration, transparency obligations, fundamental-rights impact assessment)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Legal / Govt Affairs
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3944_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3944_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3944_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3944_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3944_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-615 (ensure controlled execution — Responsible AI — Fairness, Explainability, Privacy &amp; Safety (PA-128.2).) | - operational: radar and readiness; operational: ISO 42001/NIST AI RMF alignment
Owner: AI Governance / Compliance / Legal</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
